  "body": "CRM contact creation inserts again on retries, and redundant identities have no reversible retirement workflow. Add actor-scoped request idempotency, private whole-group review and dry runs, transactional contact archival with canonical ID mappings, selective rollback, and reversible informational links for complementary contact/account records. Linking grants no ownership or permissions.\n\nAutomatic archival is limited to redundant contacts without source dependencies or unresolved fields. Credentials, roles, financial/audit relationships and ownership conflicts block execution. Dependency checks combine foreign keys, a registry of 222 model-declared Party references, and conservative legacy scalar checks. A forward migration adds model-derived archive guards, including review/approval references without foreign keys, while preserving the already-staged original migration checksum. Prior review evidence is retained; executed cases cannot be rewritten. Shared contact details remain valid, old-ID lookup keeps CRM authorization, and private history has no public API.\n\nValidation includes nine classifier/input tests with 300 generated cases, twelve CRM component tests, backend and HTTP checks, SQL concurrent replay, stale plans, field conflicts, sensitive dependencies, archive visibility, and selective undo. All 106 migrations applied and repeated on staging; its updated backup restored with ownership and private-history access controls intact. The deployed staging API passed authorization, concurrent contact retries, archive handling and rollback.\n\nA private production backup restored in a network-isolated local PostgreSQL container with all 605 table row counts matching. On that snapshot, the 106-migration batch and rehearsal of two eligible merge groups (three archives) plus one complementary link passed. After rollback/unlink, all 605 original table hashes matched. These were rehearsal operations; production cleanup has not run.\n\nThe owner classified all 17 candidate groups: 16 duplicate groups and one complementary group. Fourteen duplicate groups remain blocked by relationships or conflicting fields. Private identities and evidence are excluded from this PR. Legacy Google subject binding and other creation paths without request keys remain documented prevention gaps; this PR does not claim comprehensive recurrence prevention.\n\nPrerequisite #422 and mobile contract PRs diegueins680/TDF-mobile#92 and #95 are merged. Complete current checks and normal protected review, deploy the exact merged image, then generate fresh production dry runs and execute eligible groups individually. See docs/identity/reconciliation.md for review, merge, rollback and unlink commands. Routine undo preserves unrelated later edits and does not restore a whole database.\n",
